<title>TURKEY: Turkish Sise Cam Q1 profits rise 35.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Sise Cam Q1 profits rise 35.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   166.92 vs     299.33</p>
<p>    Net profit		    934.77 vs     688.46</p>
<p>    Net sales		     448.62 vs     239.27</p>
<p>    Operating profit	     31.99 vs	19.01</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	1,033.32 vs     710.09</p>
<p>    Interest paid		  43.38 vs	 0.02</p>
<p>    Total debts		 1,374.24 vs     958.83</p>
<p>    Equity		     14,947.27 vs   6,661.07</p>
<p>Capital 5,600.00 vs 2,300.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's glass and glassware giant T. Sise ve Cam Fabrikalari A.S. is owned 74.91 pct by T.Is Bankasi, one of the leading commercial banks.</p>
<p>Sise Cam is the parent company of a group consisting of 24 industrial and marketing firms.</p>
<p>The company will retain dividends from 1996 profits to issue a 0.5 bonus issue for one existing share from May 30 to raise its capital 8.4 trillion lira.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
